  "text_sanskrit": "लेलिह्यसे ग्रसमानः समन्ताल्- लोकान्समग्रान्वदनैर्ज्वलद्भिः । तेजोभिरापूर्य जगत्समग्रं भासस्तवोग्राः प्रतपन्ति विष्णो ॥ ११-३० ॥",
  "itrans": "lelihyase grasamAnaH samantAl.h- lokAnsamagrAnvadanairjvaladbhiH . tejobhirApUrya jagatsamagra.n bhAsastavogrAH pratapanti viShNo .. 11-30 ..",
  "translation": "On every side swallowing all the worlds with Thy fiery tongue Thou lappest (them); Thy terrible rays fill the whole world with light and make it warm, O Vishnu. (30)\nV. With light. Tejobhih. lit. powers of illuminating. (30) - \nA. Albeit he understands the nature of the Lord, His excellent attributes and activities, Arjuna requests the imparting of further knowledge of what he has not as yet understood.",
